From: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] b43: fix the rounding of the negative RSSI cal offsets

b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_cal() rounds the fine digital offset by adding half
the poll count before dividing by it. In the negative branch the closing
parenthesis of abs() is in the wrong place, so the 4 is added to the
negative value inside abs() instead of to its magnitude:

	offset[j] = -(abs(offset[j] + 4) / 8);

For every offset below -4 that rounds towards zero instead of away from
it, and the result is one LSB short. brcmsmac takes the absolute value
first, adds NPHY_RSSICAL_NPOLL / 2, divides, and negates at the end, and
the same file already gets it right twice: in the coarse stage of this
very function and in b43_nphy_rev2_rssi_cal().

An MMIO capture of wl 6.30.102.7 on a BCM6362 (N-PHY rev 8, radio 2057
rev 8) writes 0x3f to the NB RSSI multiplication coefficient and 0x3e to
the other eight. Before this change the driver computes 0x3f for all
nine; after it, all nine match the capture bit for bit.

This is not specific to radio 2057 rev 8: the expression is shared by
every N-PHY rev 3 and later, so it is deliberately not gated.

Verified: records #3723-#3740, from "PHY.WR   addr=0x01b8 val=0x003f"
Link: https://github.com/aleferri/b43-6362-wip/blob/c366cad/router-data/dsl-3580l/opinit-ch1-ch6-bw20.decoded
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmsmac/phy/phy_n.c?id=848acc8ffe1b#n22596

Signed-off-by: Alessio Ferri <alessio.ferri@mythread.it>
---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/phy_n.c
@@ -2246,7 +2246,7 @@ static void b43_nphy_rev3_rssi_cal(struct b43_wldev *dev)
 				if (j / 2 == core) {
 					offset[j] = 232 - poll_results[j];
 					if (offset[j] < 0)
-						offset[j] = -(abs(offset[j] + 4) / 8);
+						offset[j] = -((abs(offset[j]) + 4) / 8);
 					else
 						offset[j] = (offset[j] + 4) / 8;
 					b43_nphy_scale_offset_rssi(dev, 0,

Note per il repo, non per la mailing list:

  - **Non gateata**, come `0010`: e' un refuso di precedenza in un'espressione
    condivisa da ogni N-PHY rev 3+, e gatearla su rev 8 lascerebbe il difetto
    dov'e' per tutti gli altri.
  - Misura: harness in `test/`, flow `init`. I nove coefficienti passano da nove
    `0x3f` a `0x1b8 = 0x3f` piu' otto `0x3e`, identici alla cattura. Serve
    `readplans_init.h` rigenerato con `--max-len 512`: col troncamento a 64 la
    cal mediava lo specchio e il difetto non era visibile.
  - La finestra `rssi-cal` resta 1/16 e non e' questo: il port scrive ogni
    coefficiente **due volte** (prima zero, poi il valore) e intercala le read,
    il vendore scrive gli otto di fila. I valori combaciano, l'ordine no, e
    quella finestra e' posizionale.
  - Va spedita come `[PATCH]` a se', in un thread suo, con le altre due di
    `patches/mainline/`.
  - NON provata su hardware.
